  <div class="guard-do" id="guardDo"></div>
</div>

<!-- INDEPENDENT CROSS-CHECK — see the XCHK block for what it does and does not claim -->
<div class="xchk warn" id="xchk"><i>⚠</i> <b>The independent check has gone stale</b> — taken 15.0 days ago against Alpha Vantage, past the 2.5-day life this board gives it. It agreed then. It is not evidence about now.<details><summary>what was compared, and what this does not check</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Index</th><th>this board</th><th>Alpha Vantage</th><th>proxy</th><th>gap</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SPX</td><td>-0.3315%</td><td>-0.3195%</td><td>SPY</td><td>+1.2bp</td></tr><tr><td>RUT</td><td>+0.3084%</td><td>+0.3367%</td><td>IWM</td><td>+2.8bp</td></tr><tr><td>NDX</td><td>-0.3338%</td><td>-0.3357%</td><td>QQQ</td><td>-0.2bp</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Each index's session move against the same session at an unrelated vendor, via its liquid ETF proxy. That makes it a check on DIRECTION AND MAGNITUDE, not on price: an ETF tracks its index with a few basis points of slippage from fees and dividends, so a small gap is expected and is not evidence of a fault in either feed.</p><p>It says nothing about the FUTURES prices the levels are drawn on — it checks the cash indices those futures are quoted against.</p><p><b>NOT checked: HSI and VIX.</b> relay sources it from cnbc, which is unreachable from the build container. They are named here rather than quietly left out, because a check that silently skips what it cannot reach and reports a clean bill is the same defect in a new place.</p><p>It does not run itself. There is no path from this toolchain to an independent vendor without a key, and keys do not enter the build container, so it is refreshed by hand and its age is the warning.</p></details></div>

