<!-- DECISION BOARD -->
<section class="card" data-feeds="ES,RTY,NQ,YM" id="rail-decision-board">
  <div class="card-head">
    <div class="card-title">Decision board</div>
    <div class="card-sub"><details class="fwork fwork-sub"><summary>The two cards below this one, joined. Every level worth watching on both contracts, ordered not by how far away it is but by <b>how long until price can plausibly get there</b> — and, for each, which scheduled event stands in between. </summary><div class="fwork-b">A pool eight hours out is not today’s trade on current flow; it is a bet on the event that lands first. The timing is measured off the same multi-day bar archive the ladder quotes, not modelled: it says when a level enters normal reach, <b>never that price is going there</b>. Direction is the liquidity map’s job.</div></details></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <div id="decBody"><div class="cat-hd"><div class="ch-lab">Next level to come into reach</div><div class="ch-fig">RTY 3,004.3 · ~1.3h</div><div class="ch-note">Nothing scheduled stands between here and there, so this one is decided by flow. It comes into range around <b>17:17 HKT</b> (09:17Z) on the pace measured for the sessions in between. That is when it becomes <i>reachable</i> — not a claim that price goes there.</div></div><div class="dec-rail"><div class="drl-hd">The next 21 hours, both contracts on one axis</div><div class="drl-lane"><div class="drl-sym">ES</div><div class="drl-track"><span class="drl-line"></span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:14.68%">▼</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:75.00%">▲</span><span class="drl-lab" style="left:14.68%">7,708.8</span></div></div><div class="drl-lane"><div class="drl-sym">NQ</div><div class="drl-track"><span class="drl-line"></span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:7.14%">▼</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:15.08%">▲</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:69.44%">▼</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:96.83%">▲</span><span class="drl-lab" style="left:7.14%">29,461</span></div></div><div class="drl-lane"><div class="drl-sym">RTY</div><div class="drl-track"><span class="drl-line"></span><span class="drl-m now" style="left:1.50%">▲</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:6.35%">▼</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:25.40%">▲</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:26.98%">▼</span><span class="drl-lab" style="left:6.00%">3,008.0</span></div></div><div class="drl-lane"><div class="drl-sym">YM</div><div class="drl-track"><span class="drl-line"></span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:12.30%">▲</span><span class="drl-m clear" style="left:54.76%">▼</span><span class="drl-lab" style="left:12.30%">53,691</span></div></div><div class="drl-ax"><span style="left:0.00%">now</span><span style="left:28.57%">+6h</span><span style="left:57.14%">+12h</span><span style="left:85.71%">+18h</span></div><div class="drl-key">Nothing scheduled lands inside this window, so every marker here is a question of flow. Markers are levels; ▲ is above the current price and ▼ below.</div></div><div class="dec-sym"><div class="dsn">ES</div><div class="dsp">7,717.0 · European hours</div></div><div class="dec-gh" data-gh="ES:0">Clear water — nothing on the calendar lands before any of these come into reach.<span class="dghn">Everything below to 7,738.1 is the same case: getting there is a question of flow, the honest kind of level to trade against current positioning.</span></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="ES:0"><div class="dwhen">3h<span>19:02 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">7,708.8<span class="dd">-8.2 · 1.2× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 41 turns (19A+13EU+6RTH+3EV) — last touched 2h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="ES:0"><div class="dwhen">16h<span>07:42 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">7,738.1<span class="dd">+21.1 · 3.1× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 88 turns (49A+21EU+16RTH+2EV) · 24h extreme — last touched 8h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><details class="fwork dec-far" data-far="ES"><summary><b>6 more ES levels</b>, all beyond a day of normal travel — scenery, not decisions.</summary><div class="fwork-b"><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,686.3<span>-30.8 · 4.6× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 76 turns (26RTH+25EU+20A+5EV) — also the value low of the profile — last touched 12h ago</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,764.4<span>+47.4 · 7.0× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 113 turns (55A+28EU+27RTH+3EV) · stale — last touched 7.7d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,667.7<span>-49.3 · 7.3× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 67 turns (34A+17RTH+11EU+5EV) · 24h extreme · stale — last touched 1.7d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,772.5<span>+55.5 · 8.2× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The point of control of the profile</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,784.2<span>+67.2 · 10.0× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 104 turns (38A+33RTH+29EU+4EV) · stale — last touched 9.6d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">7,827.5<span>+110.5 · 16.4× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The value high of the profile</div></div></div></details><div class="invalid"><b>What breaks these times —</b> Not enough recent bars to check the pace these times assume. Treat them as the archive's typical behaviour rather than as a reading of the last hour.</div><div class="dec-sym"><div class="dsn">NQ</div><div class="dsp">29,503 · European hours</div></div><div class="dec-gh" data-gh="NQ:0">Clear water — nothing on the calendar lands before any of these come into reach.<span class="dghn">Everything below to 29,654 is the same case: getting there is a question of flow, the honest kind of level to trade against current positioning.</span></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="NQ:0"><div class="dwhen">1.5h<span>17:27 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">29,461<span class="dd">-42 · 0.9× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 24 turns (11A+8EU+4RTH+1EV) — last touched 1h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="NQ:0"><div class="dwhen">3h<span>19:07 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">29,564<span class="dd">+61 · 1.3× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 46 turns (25A+14EU+4RTH+3EV) — last touched 4h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="NQ:0"><div class="dwhen">15h<span>06:32 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">29,366<span class="dd">-137 · 2.9× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 18 turns (7RTH+7A+2EU+2EV) — last touched 11h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="NQ:0"><div class="dwhen">20h<span>12:17 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">29,654<span class="dd">+151 · 3.1× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 50 turns (26A+13RTH+10EU+1EV) · 24h extreme — last touched 8h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><details class="fwork dec-far" data-far="NQ"><summary><b>4 more NQ levels</b>, all beyond a day of normal travel — scenery, not decisions.</summary><div class="fwork-b"><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">29,286<span>-216 · 4.5× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 32 turns (14A+9RTH+6EU+3EV) — also the point of control of the profile — last touched 11h ago</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">29,761<span>+259 · 5.4× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 31 turns (15EU+8A+8RTH) · round number · stale — last touched 7.8d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">29,150<span>-353 · 7.3× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The value low of the profile</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">29,860<span>+357 · 7.4× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The value high of the profile</div></div></div></details><div class="invalid"><b>What breaks these times —</b> Not enough recent bars to check the pace these times assume. Treat them as the archive's typical behaviour rather than as a reading of the last hour.</div><div class="dec-sym"><div class="dsn">RTY</div><div class="dsp">3,007.4 · European hours</div></div><div class="dec-row now"><div class="dwhen">now<span>in reach</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">3,008.0<span class="dd">+0.6 · 0.2× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat">The point of control of the profile</div><div class="dgate">In reach right now with nothing scheduled on top of it. Whatever happens here is flow, and flow is fadeable in a way that a print is not.</div></div></div><div class="dec-gh" data-gh="RTY:0">Clear water — nothing on the calendar lands before any of these come into reach.<span class="dghn">Everything below to 3,001.0 is the same case: getting there is a question of flow, the honest kind of level to trade against current positioning.</span></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="RTY:0"><div class="dwhen">1.3h<span>17:17 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">3,004.3<span class="dd">-3.1 · 0.8× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 78 turns (40A+28RTH+8EU+2EV) · 24h extreme · stale — last touched 15h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="RTY:0"><div class="dwhen">5h<span>21:17 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">3,013.6<span class="dd">+6.2 · 1.6× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 48 turns (20A+12RTH+12EU+4EV) — last touched 5h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="RTY:0"><div class="dwhen">6h<span>21:37 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">3,001.0<span class="dd">-6.4 · 1.6× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat">The value low of the profile</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><details class="fwork dec-far" data-far="RTY"><summary><b>5 more RTY levels</b>, all beyond a day of normal travel — scenery, not decisions.</summary><div class="fwork-b"><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">2,994.4<span>-13.1 · 3.3× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 23 turns (12A+6RTH+3EU+2EV) · stale — last touched 6.5d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">3,022.1<span>+14.7 · 3.8× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 76 turns (31EU+25RTH+18A+2EV) · 24h extreme · stale — last touched 1.8d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">3,029.5<span>+22.1 · 5.7× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 69 turns (34A+22EU+9RTH+4EV) · round number · stale — last touched 6.8d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">3,038.5<span>+31.1 · 8.0× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 86 turns (33RTH+31A+18EU+4EV) · stale — last touched 6.9d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">3,064.0<span>+56.6 · 14.5× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The value high of the profile</div></div></div></details><div class="invalid"><b>What breaks these times —</b> Not enough recent bars to check the pace these times assume. Treat them as the archive's typical behaviour rather than as a reading of the last hour.</div><div class="dec-sym"><div class="dsn">YM</div><div class="dsp">53,630 · European hours</div></div><div class="dec-gh" data-gh="YM:0">Clear water — nothing on the calendar lands before any of these come into reach.<span class="dghn">Everything below to 53,476 is the same case: getting there is a question of flow, the honest kind of level to trade against current positioning.</span></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="YM:0"><div class="dwhen">2.6h<span>18:32 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">53,691<span class="dd">+61 · 1.3× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Stops both sides of</b> this level — 112 turns (48A+42EU+20RTH+2EV) — touched in the last hour</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><div class="dec-row clear" data-gh="YM:0"><div class="dwhen">12h<span>03:27 HKT</span></div><div><div class="dlvl">53,476<span class="dd">-154 · 3.2× 30m</span></div><div class="dwhat"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 108 turns (42RTH+41A+19EU+6EV) · 24h extreme · round number · stale — also the point of control of the profile — last touched 13h ago</div><div class="dgate">Clear water — flow decides this level, not the calendar.</div></div></div><details class="fwork dec-far" data-far="YM"><summary><b>5 more YM levels</b>, all beyond a day of normal travel — scenery, not decisions.</summary><div class="fwork-b"><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">53,868<span>+238 · 5.0× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 88 turns (43A+25RTH+17EU+3EV) · 24h extreme · stale — last touched 12.5d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">53,360<span>-270 · 5.6× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw">The value low of the profile</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">53,307<span>-323 · 6.7× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Sell stops below</b> this level — 40 turns (20A+11RTH+7EU+2EV) · stale — last touched 2.8d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">54,025<span>+395 · 8.2× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 81 turns (35A+27EU+17RTH+2EV) · round number · stale — also the value high of the profile — last touched 13.7d ago — stale</div></div><div class="dfr"><div class="dfp">54,150<span>+520 · 10.8× 30m</span></div><div class="dfw"><b>Buy stops above</b> this level — 34 turns (16RTH+13EU+4A+1EV) · stale — last touched 13.7d ago — stale</div></div></div></details><div class="invalid"><b>What breaks these times —</b> Not enough recent bars to check the pace these times assume. Treat them as the archive's typical behaviour rather than as a reading of the last hour.</div><details class="fwork dec-meth"><summary><b>These times are measured, and their current out-of-sample error is ES -7%, NQ -4%, RTY -3%, YM +18%.</b> The walk is fitted per contract on this archive and graded on every rebuild. None of it is a forecast of direction.</summary><div class="fwork-b"><b>How the timing is built.</b> The typical thirty-minute one-directional excursion is measured separately for Asian, European, cash and evening hours, then the clock is walked forward five minutes at a time from now, picking up whichever session's pace applies as it crosses into it. That is why a level eight times the Asian thirty-minute range away can still read a few hours: it is not waiting on hours of overnight drift, it is waiting on the cash open, and the walk finds that without being told. Distance grows as time<sup>H</sup> with <b>H</b> fitted per contract on this archive (ES 0.468, NQ 0.494, RTY 0.478, YM 0.519) rather than assumed to be the textbook 0.5. <u>The method grades itself out of sample on every rebuild — fitted on fifteen minutes to two hours, then asked to predict the four-hour excursion it never saw. Current error across all sessions: <b>ES -7%, NQ -4%, RTY -3%, YM +18%</b>.</u> <b>None of this is a forecast of direction.</b> It says when a level enters normal travelling range, never that price is going there. A level can sit in reach all day and never trade.</div></details></div>
    <!-- The same sentence the liquidity map prints, out of the same LIQ_EXCL
         object via liqExclHtml. This board's contracts are Object.keys(LIQ), so
         a contract LIQ refuses has no row here either, for that reason. -->
    <div class="liq-excl" id="decExcl"><b>Not on this map:</b> HSI — no volume at all. The relay carries HSI as the CASH INDEX, and an index has no volume at any price — there is nothing to weight a profile with. All 1,090 bars of it print a volume of zero, so every figure this card exists to produce would be a statement about an empty histogram: a point of control chosen by tie-break, a value area covering the whole range, and stop pools at turns that no contracts were traded through. Those would not be weak numbers, they would be numbers about nothing, and they would look exactly like the real ones. The tradeable instrument is the Mini-Hang Seng future, whose profile IS measured on real transacted volume — it is the Hong Kong board on the level ladder, which carries its own volume and its own pull date.</div>
