<!-- LIQUIDITY MAP -->
<section class="card" data-feeds="ES,RTY,NQ,YM" id="rail-liquidity-map">
  <div class="card-head">
    <div class="card-title">Liquidity map</div>
    <div class="card-sub"><details class="fwork fwork-sub"><summary>Where the contracts actually changed hands, built from every five-minute bar banked since the relay started. </summary><div class="fwork-b">Long bars are prices the market accepted — price returns there and stalls. Short bars are prices it refused — it crosses them fast, in both directions. The stop pools below are <b>inferred, not measured</b>: this feed carries no order book, so they are read off levels obvious enough that most desks would place stops beyond them.</div></details></div>
  </div>
